<section class="section wrap story-section" id="recognition"><p class="eyebrow">THE BIGGER PICTURE</p><h2>YOU KNOW HOW TO BUILD A BUSINESS. <em>BUT WHO'S HELPING YOU BUILD THE LIFE?</em></h2><div class="story-copy"><p>You've probably spent years making decisions that move your business forward.</p><p>Hiring the right people. Finding opportunities. Solving problems. Making sure things get done.</p><p>But here's something worth thinking about:</p><p><strong>Who's giving that same attention to the life you're building outside your business?</strong></p><p>Maybe you already have a CPA, an investment advisor, and other professionals you trust. That's great.</p><p>But who's connecting all those moving parts to what you actually want your life to look like?</p><p><strong>Because having good people working on individual pieces isn't always the same as having someone focused on the whole picture.</strong></p></div></section>
<section class="section wrap story-section clarity" id="clarity"><p class="eyebrow">CLARITY BEFORE PRODUCTS</p><h2>WHAT COULD MORE CLARITY <em>MAKE POSSIBLE?</em></h2><blockquote class="adam-quote">“Successful people make excellent decisions when they can see their options with clarity.”<cite>— Adam Kasick</cite></blockquote><div class="story-copy"><p>You've made thousands of decisions to build your business. You know how to recognize an opportunity when you see one.</p><p>But when it comes to your personal financial future, have you taken the time to see all your options?</p><p><strong>You don't need someone to make decisions for you. You need a clear picture of what's possible.</strong></p><p>I've put together nine straightforward questions to help you explore where you are, what matters most, and which decisions might deserve a closer look.</p></div><a class="button primary section-cta" href="#quiz" data-quiz-link data-placement="clarity">Take the Free Quiz →</a></section>
<section class="section wrap quiz-section" id="quiz" aria-labelledby="quiz-heading"><div class="quiz-shell"><div class="quiz-header"><div><p class="eyebrow">FREE FINANCIAL FREEDOM QUIZ</p><h2 id="quiz-heading">WHAT'S YOUR BUSINESS <em>BUILDING FOR YOU?</em></h2><p class="quiz-promise">Nine questions. About three minutes. No right or wrong answers. No email required.</p></div></div><div id="quiz-progress" class="quiz-progress"><span id="step-label">Question 1 of 9</span><div class="track"><i id="progress-fill"></i></div></div><div id="quiz-content"></div></div><section id="results" hidden aria-live="polite"></section></section>
<section class="section wrap story-section how-help" id="how-help"><p class="eyebrow">HOW I HELP</p><h2>I MAY HAVE A FEW MORE GOOD IDEAS FOR YOU, <em>BUT WHAT YOU REALLY NEED IS SOMEONE TO HELP MAKE THEM ALL HAPPEN.</em></h2><div class="story-copy"><p>You've probably got a list of financial things you've been meaning to get around to.</p><p>Ideas you've had. Conversations you need to have. Decisions you know deserve attention.</p><p>The problem usually isn't a shortage of good ideas.</p><p><strong>It's finding the time to turn them into action.</strong></p><p>And when you finally have some free time, shouldn't you get to enjoy it?</p><p>That's where I come in.</p><p>My job is to bring ideas worth considering, help connect your financial professionals, and keep important decisions moving forward—so you can spend more of your time doing what you actually want to do.</p><h3>Think of me as your financial general contractor.</h3><p>Your CPA, attorney, insurance professional, and investment advisor each have important responsibilities. I help you see how their work fits together and who owns the next step. Each professional remains responsible for advice within their own specialty.</p></div><a class="button outline section-cta" href="https://calendly.com/adam-riplwealth/20-minute-zoom-meeting" data-book data-book-type="how-help">Book a 20-Minute Call With Adam →</a></section>
<section class="section wrap about" id="about"><div class="about-photo family-photo"><img src="/money-at-work/images/adam-family-original.jpg" alt="Adam with his family" width="609" height="640" loading="lazy"/></div><div><p class="eyebrow">MEET ADAM</p><h2>I'VE BEEN ON YOUR <em>SIDE OF THE TABLE.</em></h2><p>I've spent much of my career building and running businesses. I know what it's like to have a hundred things competing for your attention—and still feel like there are important things you haven't gotten around to.</p><p>I also know that the point of building a successful business isn't just to keep building a bigger business.</p><p><strong>It's what that success makes possible for you and the people you care about.</strong></p><p>Today, as a wealth manager with RIPL Wealth, I work with business owners to bring good ideas to the table, connect the financial pieces, and help turn important decisions into action.</p><p>I don't expect you to trust me because of a website or a few clever questions.</p><p><strong>I'd rather earn that trust through a conversation.</strong></p><div class="credential"><strong>Adam Kasick · Wealth Manager, RIPL Wealth</strong><p>Business owner and financial professional. Investment advisory services are provided through RIPL Wealth, LLC, a registered investment adviser.</p><p><a href="https://adviserinfo.sec.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Verify adviser registration ↗</a></p></div></div></section>
